<section class="w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto py-12 px-4 sm:px-6">
  <div class="glass-panel-elevated rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 border border-white/10 space-y-10">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="text-left space-y-2">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-400 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider border border-amber-500/20">
        <span>📖 Vedic & Gemological Guide</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white font-display" data-i18n="explainerTitle">
        Understanding Ratti vs Carat: The Complete Guide
      </h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm max-w-2xl leading-relaxed" data-i18n="explainerSubtitle">
        Why do astrologers prescribe in Ratti while certified jewelers and gem testing laboratories (GIA, IGI) weigh in Carats?
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3 Core Concept Cards Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <!-- Card 1: What is Ratti -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-black/40 border border-white/5 space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-amber-400 text-lg">
          🌱
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display">1. The Origin of Ratti</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Historically, a <strong>Ratti</strong> was based on the red-and-black seed of the <em>Gunja</em> plant (Abrus precatorius), known for its uniform mass of approximately 180 to 182 milligrams. Vedic Ayurvedic and astrological literature universally uses Ratti for planetary remedy prescriptions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 2: What is Carat -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-black/40 border border-white/5 space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-blue-500/10 border border-blue-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-blue-400 text-lg">
          ⚖️
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display">2. The Metric Carat (Ct)</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Adopted internationally in 1907, the <strong>Metric Carat</strong> is an absolute SI unit of mass where <strong>1 Carat = 200 milligrams (0.200 grams)</strong>. All international gem testing laboratories (GIA, IGI, AGS) issue certification certificates strictly in Carats.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 3: The 0.91 Conversion Law -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-black/40 border border-white/5 space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400 text-lg">
          📐
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display">3. Pakka vs Sunee Standard</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          In certified trade, <strong>1 Pakka Ratti = 0.91 Carats (182 mg)</strong>. In local unorganized markets, some jewelers use a loose rounded <strong>0.90 ratio</strong> (Sunee/Kachha). Buying by Pakka Ratti ensures you never underpay or under-dose your gemstone remedy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Astrological Sawa Insight Box -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-500/10 via-black/40 to-black/60 border border-amber-500/20 space-y-3">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-amber-300 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>✨</span> Why Astrologers Prescribe "Sawa" Weights (5.25, 6.25, 7.25 Ratti)
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
        In Vedic numerology and astrological gem therapy, fractions have vibrational significance:
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2 text-xs">
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-black/50 border border-amber-500/20 space-y-1">
          <span class="font-bold text-amber-400">Sawa (+0.25) — Auspicious</span>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-zinc-400">Represents expansion, growth, and ascending energy (Vridhi).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-black/50 border border-blue-500/20 space-y-1">
          <span class="font-bold text-blue-400">Saadhe (+0.50) — Neutral</span>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-zinc-400">Represents balance, stability, and peaceful maintenance (Sthirta).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-black/50 border border-rose-500/20 space-y-1">
          <span class="font-bold text-rose-400">Paune (+0.75) — Avoided</span>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-zinc-400">Considered incomplete or decaying in orthodox North Indian tradition.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
